{"reply":"You could put it this way:

“Part of me wants to be honest immediately, because taking responsibility matters to me. Another part wants to repair the damage quietly, before anyone can see me differently. They’re both trying to protect something—but they’re asking for opposite kinds of courage.”

Or, more simply: “I’m torn between being accountable in public and being forgiven in private.”","memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

